WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.635 --> 00:00:03.052
(soft music)

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:08.910
- I was delighted to serve

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:10.560
as Co-chair of the President's Committee

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.640
on Diversity, Inclusion, and Belonging.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.630
Their work is very important,

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.610
for our society and for our University,

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:20.310
but it's not easy.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.950
I was tremendously
impressed by the expertise,

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.920
generosity and thoughtful contribution

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.900
of each member of the committee.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:28.520
Each one of them brought a different kind

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.430
of expertise to the table,

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.440
their knowledge and experience,

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.550
their commitment to deep discussions

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.840
and their collective wisdoms allowed

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:37.910
us to continue our work

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:40.890
during a very challenging
spring and summer,

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.200
and to produce a report
for President Salovey,

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.233
that I think we can all be proud of.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:49.730
The report builds on previous
University initiatives

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.750
and proposes a forward looking framework.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.810
I am confident,

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.220
that the group's recommendation

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:57.713
will serve here well,
for many years to come.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.700
- I'm Ann Kurth the Dean of
the Yale School of Nursing.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.560
It's a good moment to have
this report coming out,

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.860
the COVID-19 crisis,

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.270
has really demonstrated

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.340
the racial disparities in health care

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.330
that black indigenous people of color

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.840
and other populations have suffered

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.783
from in our country for many years.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.940
This is a timely moment,

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.950
it's a pivotal one,

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:24.030
the nation is calling for justice

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.940
and Yale can respond,

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.590
Higher education needs to
be a part of this movement.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.040
At the School of Nursing,

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:33.100
we are making Diversity,
Equity, Inclusion,

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.240
Belonging, and Anti-racism work a priority

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.620
because we must reflect
the communities we serve

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:39.970
in the way that we educate,

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.533
practice and conduct research,

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:45.920
much learning has to happen

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.840
and I'm learning also,

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:51.030
white people, must listen with intention

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.420
to our BiPAP colleagues,

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.423
friends, students, and loved ones,

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.400
we've spent 400 years
centering white voices,

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.320
now we must center the voice stories

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.680
and narratives of our BiPAP
members of our population

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:09.343
and support, their needs to thrive.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:14.540
Nothing less, would be right

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:18.350
as an Institution and
as a larger community,

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:20.220
Yale as always can lead by example

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.600
and take bold action,

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.600
this report is a step in that direction.

00:02:25.382 --> 00:02:27.650
- My name is Darin Latimore,

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:31.140
I am deputy Dean of
Diversity, Equity, Inclusion

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.210
at the School of Medicine.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.840
I first wanna say it was an honor

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.350
to be on the President's Committee.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:42.330
Each of us, looks at these
issues through our own lenses

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:45.630
however, it was immediately clear

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:49.720
that all of us felt a strong commitment

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:54.493
to creating a just environment
at Yale University.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.920
I also wanna thank our community,

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.540
many of us interviewed
students, staff, and faculty

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:06.220
in order to get the
information that we needed

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:09.643
to create the most robust plan possible.

00:03:11.526 --> 00:03:14.370
I'm very grateful that
I was on the Committee

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.730
because at the same time,

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:18.870
I was actually developing a strategic plan

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.170
for the School of Medicine.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:23.270
It was really helpful

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.420
to be able to see what the University

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.520
is doing in the DEI space,

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.460
as I created my plan

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:31.840
because I wanted to make
sure that the strategies

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.640
that I use at the Medical School,

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.250
are in line with the strategies

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:37.730
that the University as a whole are using,

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.690
and the outcomes that I am measuring

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.760
are the same ones that the University

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.743
as a whole are measuring.

00:03:44.973 --> 00:03:46.530
I like to say,

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:49.000
when we're all going
in the same direction,

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.060
working together, there's
a much better chance

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:54.140
that we'll get the outcome that we want.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:58.230
- Hello, my name is Weili Cheng,

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:02.680
I am the Executive Director of
the Yale Alumni Association.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.370
The mission of the Yale
Alumni Association States,

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:09.950
Our character, strengths and
values come from our diversity

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:13.920
and our commitment to a culture
of inclusion and equity.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.400
Our mission is to enhance and renew

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.480
the lifelong Yale
experience for all alumni,

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.790
whoever they are and wherever they may be.

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:25.773
So who are our Alumni?

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:29.070
Our Alumni Community is a diverse group

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:32.720
that spans generations, identities,

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:36.220
Yale affiliations, and interests.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:37.330
So our core value

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:41.283
of the Yale Alumni
Association is Inclusion.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.653
What does Inclusion mean?

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.700
It means that we strive
for full engagement

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.923
and a sense of belonging among our Alumni.

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:54.410
All of our Alumni have had the privilege

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:57.770
of experiences and opportunities at,

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.853
and because of Yale,

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.540
these experiences and
opportunities influence

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.410
our choices and decisions and in turn,

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.030
these choices and decisions

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:13.623
can positively impact our communities,

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.210
especially if there is an understanding

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:21.163
of Diversity, Equity,
Inclusion, and Belonging.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:24.900
At this moment in time,

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.630
we have an opportunity

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.930
and an obligation to advance

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.330
these important principles,

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:36.040
they are priorities for
the Yale Alumni Association

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:37.653
and for the University.

00:05:38.775 --> 00:05:41.220
- I remember so clearly those meetings

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:44.020
after we received our charge
from President Salovey,

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:46.390
to shape the next phase
of University's work

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:48.360
on Diversity, Equity and Inclusion,

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.010
as well as Belonging.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:51.240
What a great committee,

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.693
and we had some really
amazing conversations.

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:56.740
So many members of the committee,

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:58.980
have expertise in these areas

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:00.730
or have been citizens of the University

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.070
for a very long time,

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:04.230
so they understand our culture.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:07.380
We talked often about how this work,

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:09.773
is more of a marathon and not a sprint.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:12.560
We reviewed the work,

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.210
that has been done by generations

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:17.010
of students and faculty, staff, and alumni

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.490
We talked to a lot of people on campus,

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:21.900
and we compiled a pretty amazing list

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.220
of every project that's currently underway

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:26.620
or being planned in the schools

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:28.320
and then the Administrative Units.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:33.260
I began to think of this
whole project differently,

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:34.880
the Committee's recommendations

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:36.970
and the President's priorities,

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:39.070
not so much as a marathon,

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:41.463
but as a part of a relay race.

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:46.290
Individuals complete marathons, right?

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:50.030
But teams actually compete in relay races

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:55.030
and each person, leg, has
its individual contribution

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:56.873
that's unique to that person.

00:06:58.170 --> 00:06:59.990
So the Committee's work,

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:02.053
is really about passing the baton,

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:04.690
the baton, if you will,

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:08.520
toward a more inclusive, a more diverse,

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:09.620
a more excellent Yale,

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:14.230
a Yale where every member,
feels a sense of belonging

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:18.930
and that baton, has a common vision,

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:21.500
a guiding principle and goals

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.220
to align the work that's being done,

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:25.780
work that spans schools

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:28.263
and generations, identities, and views.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:31.870
That baton also includes actions

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:34.430
for the first five
years, of this next phase

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.800
and all of this, by the
way, can be found online.

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:44.010
Yes, we're moving into the
next phase of this race,

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:47.730
and we have the ability
to create real change

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:50.003
and together, that is what we will do.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:54.020
We all belong here, we all belong to Yale.

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:56.960
So let's make sure that
we show up for ourselves

00:07:56.960 --> 00:07:57.933
and for each other,

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.763
let's make sure that this
part of the journey, counts.

